{
  "$comment": "#EDE-95: genUI search marks (Text, Markdown, MessageBubble, Row `highlight` {query, current?, before?}), THE rule src/highlight.ts implements and every renderer + count twin replays (Rust eui-core `text_highlight`, Swift `TextHighlight`, Kotlin `TextHighlight`). FOLD: each Unicode scalar of text and query → canonical decomposition (NFD), lower case, combining marks dropped (U+0300–036F, 1AB0–1AFF, 1DC0–1DFF, 20D0–20FF, FE20–FE2F); `ß` stays `ß`. A match = the folded query found in the folded text, left to right, never overlapping; it spans the original scalars its folded characters came from plus the combining marks right after; a query that folds to nothing matches nothing. `cases`: `ranges` = UTF-16 offsets [start, end) into `text`, `matches` = those slices. `currentCases`: the LOCAL current index of a node = `current` minus the matches `before` has (none = -1; negative or inside `before` = -1). `markdownCases`: a Markdown searches each block of its markdown-render.json normal form apart (a paragraph, heading, list item or quote = its runs joined; each table cell, header first, row by row; never a code block, image, attachment or rule), a link by its label never its target, a host chip as ONE U+FFFC that no query matches (chips stay whole); `count` = the node's matches (what a host numbers), `matches` = their text in order. Painting: `$color.match` behind each match, `$color.matchCurrent` behind the current one; the text keeps its colour.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "case-insensitive",
      "text": "Hello world, hello again",
      "query": "hello",
      "ranges": [
        [
          0,
          5
        ],
        [
          13,
          18
        ]
      ],
      "matches": [
        "Hello",
        "hello"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "accents in the text",
      "text": "Café crème brûlée",
